  "stem": "If \\(\\frac{x + 4}{3} - \\frac{x - 1}{2} = 1\\), what is the value of \\(x\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "5"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Multiply every term by 6: \\(2(x + 4) - 3(x - 1) = 6\\).",
    "Distribute: \\(2x + 8 - 3x + 3 = 6\\), so \\(-x + 11 = 6\\).",
    "Then \\(x = 5\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x = symbols('x')\nsol = solve(Eq((x + 4)/3 - (x - 1)/2, 1), x)\nassert sol == [5]\nassert [Rational(a) for a in spr_answers] == sol",
